\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. When Thy soldiers take their swords,
\par When they speak the solemn words,
\par When they kneel before Thee here,
\par Feeling Thee, their Father, near:
\par These Thy children, Lord, defend,
\par To their help Thy Spirit  send.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. When the world's sharp strife is nigh,
\par When they hear the battle-cry,
\par When they rush into the fight;
\par Knowing not temptation's might:
\par These Thy children, Lord, defend,
\par To their zeal Thy wisdom lend.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. When their hearts are lifted high
\par With success or victory,
\par When  they feel the conqueror's pride-
\par Lest they grow self-satisfied-
\par These Thy children, Lord, defend,
\par Teach their souls to Thee to bend.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. When the vows that they have made,
\par When the prayers that they have prayed,
\par Shall be fading from their hearts,
\par When their first warm faith departs:
\par These Thy children, Lord, defend,
\par keep them faithful to the end.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
\par }

